\import{base-macros}

\p{\code{\verb~|rlvm-ref~} is a direct implementation of the official kernel: inference and checking with every restriction, weak head normal forms with delta, iota, K, structure eta, projections, quotients, the Nat functions and String literals, and definitional equality in the official order with lazy delta by hints, proof irrelevance, eta and the official caches. It serves as an engine and gives admission its kernel operations. The first publication had 92 fixture tests green on the real store. Run at kernel level over the arena tests, with inductive records trusted and no admission, it accepts all 138 good tests including the 35 performance tests, rejects the 69 bad tests whose fault lies in a definition, theorem, axiom or duplicate name, and declines none. The depth limit was raised to \code{\verb~|2^21~} levels because three performance tests need 524,300.}

\p{Detail: \src{rlvm-ref/README.md}. Commit \commit{45563d9}. Session: [foundation modules and the reference pipeline](ses-BQZM). Related: [the reference engine](design-reference-engine).}
